# ─── Real-Time WebSockets & ASGI (Daphne / Channels) ───────────────────────────
# Upper caps added. `>=` with no ceiling made these three the least reproducible
# lines in the file: a clean install could pull a future major (channels 5,
# daphne 5) with breaking changes onto the exact commit that last worked. The cap
# pins the major the code is written against while still allowing minor/patch
# security fixes inside the 4.x line.
daphne>=4.1.2,<5
channels>=4.1.0,<5
channels-redis>=4.2.0,<5

# ─── AI Integration ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The installed and tested SDK is 2.22.0. The previous cap (<0.4, with a comment
# that said "0.8.x") was stale: the code uses only the stable
# genai.Client / google.genai.types surface, but the cap had drifted so far from
# what every build and test actually ran against that a fresh install would have
# silently downgraded the AI integration to an unvalidated SDK. Pinned exactly
# to reproduce the known-good build; bump deliberately after testing the newer
# client.
google-genai==2.22.0
# pydantic is a transitive dependency of google-genai (>=2.12.5,<3). Left
# unpinned, the resolver selects the newest 2.x — which is currently a
# pre-release (2.14.0b2). Pin it to the stable release the build was validated
# against.
pydantic==2.12.5

